# Scroll Area Pattern

Never use native browser scrollbars (`overflow-auto`, `overflow-y-auto`, `overflow-x-auto`) for product UI panels. Use `ScrollArea` from `@repo/ui` instead.

## When to use

- Sidebars and nav lists
- Main content regions inside app shells
- Dialogs, sheets, popovers with long content
- Tables, card lists, and any fixed-height panel that can overflow

## Pattern

Give the scroll parent a constrained height (`h-full`, `h-*`, or `min-h-0 flex-1` inside a flex column), then wrap content in `ScrollArea`:

```tsx
import { ScrollArea } from "@repo/ui"

// Flex child that should scroll
<div className="min-h-0 flex-1">
  <ScrollArea className="h-full">
    <div className="p-4">{/* content */}</div>
  </ScrollArea>
</div>

// Fixed-height panel
<ScrollArea className="h-72 rounded-md border">
  {/* content */}
</ScrollArea>
```

## Avoid

```tsx
// ❌ Native scrollbar
<nav className="overflow-y-auto">...</nav>
<main className="flex-1 overflow-y-auto">...</main>
```

## Notes

- `ScrollArea` is exported from `@repo/ui` (`packages/client/ui/src/components/ui/scroll-area.tsx`).
- Demo lives on the design system page under **Scroll Area**.
- Body/document scroll for full pages is fine; this rule is for in-app panels.
